b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays (5.2), procedures (5.4), the for statement with step-until and while elements (4.6), conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8), and the holding of each relation until enough of its places are known, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: c1 c2 c3, the integers of R1, x + y + z = c1, R2, y + z = c2, and R3, z = c3, in the order the problem writes the relations, whatever the instance's order;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P07a, every instance. Integer unknowns x, y, z. One stage: R1, R2 and R3, posed in the instance's order, which the instance line gives as the codes of the relations by their place as written. Each unknown is a Boolean that says whether it has a value and an integer that holds it. Each relation is held as posed until enough of its places are known, when it gives the remaining place its value or is tested. Every held relation is examined in the order posed, again and again, until a whole pass gives no unknown a value;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, c1, c2, c3, xv, yv, zv, held, pass, x1, x2, x3;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ xk, yk, zk, r1, r2, r3, changed, inconsistent;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ ord[1:3];

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine1;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of R1, x + y + z = c1: with two places known it gives the third its value, with all three known it is tested;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    x1 := x1 + 1;
    i̲f̲ xk ∧ yk ∧ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ xv + yv + zv ≠ c1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r1 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ yk ∧ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ xv := c1 - yv - zv; xk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r1 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ xk ∧ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ yv := c1 - xv - zv; yk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r1 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ xk ∧ yk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ zv := c1 - xv - yv; zk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r1 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine1;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine2;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of R2, y + z = c2;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    x2 := x2 + 1;
    i̲f̲ yk ∧ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ yv + zv ≠ c2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ yk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ zv := c2 - yv; zk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ yv := c2 - zv; yk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r2 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine2;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ examine3;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of R3, z = c3;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    x3 := x3 + 1;
    i̲f̲ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ zv ≠ c3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ zv := c3; zk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    r3 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ examine3;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ propagate;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ every held relation is examined, in the order posed, again and again until a whole pass gives no unknown a value;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ pass := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ changed d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      changed := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ 3 d̲o̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲f̲ ord[j] = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine1 e̲n̲d̲
        e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ord[j] = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine2 e̲n̲d̲
        e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ord[j] = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ examine3 e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ propagate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ uname(u);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ u; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ u;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the name of unknown u, 1 for x, 2 for y, 3 for z;
  i̲f̲ u = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ u = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`y') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`z');

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ place(known, v, u);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ known, v, u; b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ known; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v, u;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a place of a relation, its value if known, else the name of its unknown;
  i̲f̲ known t̲h̲e̲n̲ print(v) e̲l̲s̲e̲ uname(u);

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ state(known, v, inheld, u);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ known, v, inheld, u; b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ known, inheld; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v, u;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an unknown, as its value, or held by a relation, or free;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    uname(u);
    i̲f̲ known t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ inheld t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free')
  e̲n̲d̲ state;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ relations;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the relations held, in the order posed, separated by commas, with the values known put in their places;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ first;
    first := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ 3 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ ord[j] = 1 ∧ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲f̲ ¬first t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
        place(xk, xv, 1); PRINTTEXT(` + '); place(yk, yv, 2); PRINTTEXT(` + '); place(zk, zv, 3);
        PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(c1); first := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
      e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ord[j] = 2 ∧ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲f̲ ¬first t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
        place(yk, yv, 2); PRINTTEXT(` + '); place(zk, zv, 3); PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(c2); first := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
      e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ord[j] = 3 ∧ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲f̲ ¬first t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
        place(zk, zv, 3); PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(c3); first := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ relations;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, whose codes are the instance's order, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ ord[i] := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants;
  c1 := read; c2 := read; c3 := read;
  xk := yk := zk := inconsistent := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
  x1 := x2 := x3 := 0;
  r1 := r2 := r3 := t̲r̲u̲e̲;

  propagate;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: every unknown, and the relations still held;
  i̲f̲ ¬inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    PRINTTEXT(`[answer]');
    state(xk, xv, r1, 1); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
    state(yk, yv, r1 ∨ r2, 2); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
    state(zk, zv, r1 ∨ r2 ∨ r3, 3);
    i̲f̲ r1 ∨ r2 ∨ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, where '); relations e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the relations held, the values known, how many relations wait, and how often each was examined;
  held := (i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0);
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  i̲f̲ inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`held relations: ');
  i̲f̲ held = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none') e̲l̲s̲e̲ relations;
  NLCR;
  i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind x]'); print(xv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
  i̲f̲ yk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind y]'); print(yv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
  i̲f̲ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind z]'); print(zv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
  i̲f̲ held > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended held-relations '); print(held); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations R1-examined '); print(x1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations R2-examined '); print(x2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations R3-examined '); print(x3); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
